+|---|---|---|---|
+| interior depth at 0.5 / 1.0 / 1.5 / 2.0 s (yd) | 0.20 / 0.80 / 1.70 / 2.70 | 0.10 / 0.50 / 1.10 / 2.00 | 0.40 / 0.85 / 1.40 / 1.75 |
+| tackle depth at 2.0 s (yd) | 3.70 | 4.00 | 4.00 |
+| pressured, % of dropbacks | ~33 | 33.9 / 33.1 | 32.1 / 32.0 |
+| interior DL/LB pressure | ~9.8 | 12.8 / 14.1 | 10.7 / 10.8 |
+| edge level/in-front pressure | — | 6.5 / 6.2 | 5.6 / 6.7 |
+| sacked | — | 6 / 6 | 7 / 5 |
+| held pair, rusher across his line to the QB, 1.0–1.5 / 1.5–2.5 s (yd/s) | 0.91 / 0.89 | 1.04 / 1.26; 0.80 / 1.11 | 0.68 / 0.68; 0.59 / 0.66 |
+| held pair, rusher toward the QB, 1.5–2.5 s | 0.85 | 1.00 / 1.00 | 0.30 / 0.19 |
+| held rusher speed, 1.5–2.5 s | 1.58 | 2.06 / 2.00 | 1.12 / 1.00 |
+| first release by 1.0 / 2.0 s, never | 43 / 60 / 37 | 31 / 47 / 47; 30 / 45 / 51 | 26 / 33 / 63; 27 / 34 / 64 |
+
+**What it does:**
+- The interior lineman now gets off the ball. He meets the rusher at about the NFL's depth by 1.0 s (0.85 against 0.80;
+  0.50 off), and the held pair no longer slides.
+- Pressure and sacks are about unchanged overall. Interior pressure falls a little, and the edge is unchanged.
+- **Late, the pocket is shallow:** 1.75 against 2.70 yd at 2.0 s. Is that the rusher's drive, or the set's second
+  phase? Mostly the drive (`set-retreat.mts`, seed 11 × 4, LG / C / RG on dropbacks):
+  - Past the short set he asks for little retreat: 0.39 / 0.43 / 0.46 yd/s at 1.0–1.5 / 1.5–2.0 / 2.0–2.5 s.
+  - He is carried back at 1.19 / 0.96 / 0.79 yd/s, so half to two thirds of the late ground is the rusher's drive.
+  - Off, his own request ran 1.6–1.8 yd/s late. That request was the old second phase: the live QB's drop, read through
+    the clearance.
+  - The NFL's held rusher still moves at 1.58 yd/s late, ours at 1.0–1.1; toward the QB, 0.85 against 0.2–0.3. The
+    held rusher asks for 4.5 yd/s at the QB and is stopped.
+  - So the late gap is how hard the pair drives through his anchor. It is not a request we are missing. Adding a
+    "give ground" request would be the opposite of the coaching.
+  - Releases are now rarer than the NFL's (never released 63% against 37%), consistent with the same stall.
+- **Bull rush** (`rep-rolls.mts`, seed 11 × 4):
+  - Sheds a bull opened: off 14 of 100 sheds in 379 dropbacks, giving 13 pressures. SET_SPOT: 7 of 77 sheds in 344
+    dropbacks, giving 4 pressures.
+  - Carried back beyond his request on reps with a bull: 0.34 → 0.30 yd/s for the stronger rushers (top third) and
+    0.14 → 0.14 for the weaker.
+  - Interior gain on the QB with no move in flight: 0.22 → 0.08 yd per 0.5 s.
+  - The bull still moves the blocker by strength. It opens fewer clean wins because he meets it set, not standing.
+
+## The hand-fight residual, re-read on top
+
+The full hand fight is `RUSH_HANDS + FITTED_HANDS + PASS_OFF + BLOCK_ANTICIPATE + FIGHT_MENU`. The card's residual was
+twofold: the engaged rusher's speed rose late, and the orbit was half kept.
+
+| (s11 / s23) | NFL | hand fight | hand fight + SET_SPOT |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| orbit p50, 0.5–1.0 / 1.0–1.5 / 1.5–2.5 s (deg) | 25 / 34 / 39 | 13 / 20 / 34; 13 / 23 / 35 | 16 / 27 / 31; 17 / 32 / 33 |
+| engaged rusher speed p50, 0.5–1.0 / 1.0–1.5 / 1.5–2.5 s | 2.50 / 2.06 / 1.80 | 1.80 / 2.50 / 2.55 (both) | 1.80 / 1.58 / 1.58; 1.80 / 1.80 / 1.58 |
+| held pair, rusher across, 1.5–2.5 s | 0.89 | 2.24; 2.07 | 1.10; 1.12 |
+| first release by 1.0 / 2.0 s, never | 43 / 60 / 37 | 38 / 58 / 38; 49 / 67 / 30 | 41 / 54 / 44; 52 / 63 / 35 |
+| interior pressure, % of dropbacks | ~9.8 | 16.3 / 16.1 | 19.0 / 17.1 |
+| pressured / sacked | ~33 / — | 38.7 / 38.9; 8 / 6 | 40.9 / 39.0; 10 / 7 |
+
+**Read:**
+- With the set reference under it, the hand fight's late speed-up is gone: 1.58 against the NFL's 1.80, where it was
+  2.55.
+- The orbit moves toward the NFL's, and releases are close to the NFL's on both seeds.
+- What remains is interior pressure. It runs about twice the NFL's, with or without SET_SPOT. It is the hand fight's
+  own come-off (section 17), not the set's.
+
+## Identity
+
+- Off: seed 999 equals engine-68 (`763db5c8fa3d4671`).
+- `SET_SPOT=1`: `df3dbe9f2cb3ff09` on the Flex branch, against engine-68.
+- The patch's own identity against engine-69 is in its commit message.
+
+
